The linear equation of state gives explicit density and enthalpy coordinates. On a compact boundaryless slice, the sourced Gauss constraint is incompatible with a charge-per-number-density field of one strict sign; the counterexample includes a spatially uniform candidate and checks its pointwise Gauss failure.
